The Windows release includes Xpdf pdftotext 4.06 by Glyph & Cog, LLC, built from
unmodified source with optional libraries disabled. It is distributed under GPL v3.
Xpdf COPYING, COPYING3, README and the unmodified upstream source archive
xpdf-4.06.tar.gz accompany the binary in resources/xpdf. The official source is
https://www.xpdfreader.com/download.html. The executable's distribution notices
and build instructions are authoritative. Preserve them when redistributing.

resources/xpdf/BUILD.json identifies the source and binary hashes, compiler and
SDK used for this release. scripts/build-pdf.ps1 in the accompanying SCUPA source
archive is the build recipe. The target links Xpdf's goo/fofi libraries and the
Microsoft C/C++ runtime; it does not link Qt, FreeType, libpaper, lcms or fontconfig.

Electron, Chromium, Playwright and their dependencies retain their own licenses.
Electron's LICENSE and LICENSES.chromium.html ship with the desktop runtime.
This software uses libraries from the FFmpeg project under LGPL-2.1-or-later.
The replaceable ffmpeg.dll is part of Electron. Its corresponding source,
Electron patches, Opus dependency, build materials, LGPL text and provenance
are included in resources/ffmpeg; read that directory's README.md for build
and replacement instructions. SCUPA does not restrict reverse engineering or
modification of that library. Preserve these materials when redistributing.

Sync uses separately installed Edge or Chrome; no sync browser is bundled.
Node dependencies retain package licenses inside app.asar. A source release
includes the lockfile and build recipe.
